<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistani forex market shut due to holiday.</title>
<headline>Pakistani forex market shut due to holiday.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-12-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Foreign exchange establishments remained closed on Wednesday due to a national public holiday on the occasion of Pakistan's founder Mohammad Ali Jinnah's birthday, one dealer said.</p>
<p>The foreign exchange market would reopen on Thursday, the dealer said.</p>
<p>On Tuesday, the rupee closed at 42.05 to the dollar in the kerb market, the dealer said.</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
